From b52d9a0dd7f9ec58b86775adcb1d8aa7d4322ad5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Javier Maestro <jjmaestro@ieee.org>
Date: Fri, 31 Jul 2026 01:47:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix(rules): stop registering the app jar as a
 quarkus_test app root

quarkus_test cannot run against an application that declares @QuarkusMain:
augmentation fails with the application's own main class reported twice,
"More than one @QuarkusMain method found with name '': X and X".

OUTPUT_SOURCES_DIR was built from the transitive local classpath, so it
carried the application jar as well as the test jar. In test mode the
application jar is already the model's application artifact, because
collapseTestRoot folds the test root into the application, so passing it
again as an application root indexes every class in it twice.

The duplication was there for every quarkus_test target. It is invisible
for beans and REST resources and only becomes an error for @QuarkusMain,
whose uniqueness check counts annotation instances.

Only the test roots need to arrive through OUTPUT_SOURCES_DIR.
---
 quarkus/private/quarkus_test_impl.bzl | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/quarkus/private/quarkus_test_impl.bzl b/quarkus/private/quarkus_test_impl.bzl
index f9e09b9..85824f3 100644
--- a/quarkus/private/quarkus_test_impl.bzl
+++ b/quarkus/private/quarkus_test_impl.bzl
@@ -107,7 +107,7 @@ def _test_impl(ctx, integration):
     # roots exposes their @ConfigRoot classes to both classloaders (SRCFG00027).
     cp_file = write_runfiles_paths_file(ctx, "_cp.txt", runtime_classpath, ":")
     ext_rt_jars = collect_extension_runtime_jars(ctx.attr.deps)
-    direct_jars_file = write_runfiles_paths_file(ctx, "_direct_jars.txt", collect_local_app_jars(ctx.attr.deps, runtime_classpath, ext_rt_jars), ",")
+    direct_jars_file = write_runfiles_paths_file(ctx, "_direct_jars.txt", collect_local_app_jars(ctx.attr.deps, depset(), ext_rt_jars), ",")
 
     tool_jar = ctx.file.quarkifier_tool
     java_runtime = ctx.attr._java_runtime[java_common.JavaRuntimeInfo]
